    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (82.95), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against starters with xERAs near or above 4.60. **Gunnar Henderson** is our primary target, as he faces a soft matchup against Avila and maximizes his value through an elite leadoff position and strong park factors. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Andy Pages** (74.02) are primed for high-efficiency production; **Jackson Merrill** leverages a dynamic platoon advantage against Bieber, while **Andy Pages** benefits from a slow-delivering pitcher, which significantly boosts his stolen base upside\u2014a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of the SB category.\n\nThe most challenging decision today was leaving **Heliot Ramos** (51.67) on the bench. Despite a solid score and the benefit of a leadoff spot, he is hampered by a matchup against Gordon, whose xERA of 3.69 represents a significantly tougher hurdle than those facing our starting outfielders. While **Heliot Ramos** offers high-upside speed, he narrowly missed the cut because the current outfield configuration of **Kyle Tucker**, **Cole Carrigg**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Josh Lowe** provides a more balanced combination of park-adjusted power and projected efficiency. \n\nWe are monitoring the risk profile of **Sam Antonacci** (55.00) closely today. While he secures a leadoff spot, his negative platoon split against Lopez, J results in a lower efficiency score compared to his peers. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** (60.10) remains a recommended start, as his high recency score and the favorable SP skill gap against Leahy outweigh the minor park-induced penalty. No extreme weather threats exist today, but managers should note that the SB-heavy profile of **Josh Lowe** and **Andy Pages** makes them our most sensitive assets to game flow; should they fall behind early, their green-light status on the basepaths may fluctuate.",
